  "claim_short": "1711.08906 Hamhalter Kalenda Measures of weak non-compactness in spaces of nuclear operators Theorem 2.1(c) page 5 asks whether constant 2 is optimal in chi(A) <= inf finite C,D sup nuclear norm ||T-P_C T Q_D|| <= 2 chi(A). Candidate full solution: no; 2 improves uniformly to 3/2. For coordinate projections P,Q, sign isometries U=2P-I and V=2Q-I give exact identity T-PTQ=(3T-UT-TV-UTV)/4 and complement norm <=3/2...",
